WEBVTT

00:16.355 --> 00:17.379
Morning!

00:17.590 --> 00:18.591
Becky!

00:18.591 --> 00:19.692
Hey!

00:19.692 --> 00:22.127
Look at you, you seem to be in
a good mood for a change!

00:22.428 --> 00:23.996
Don't say "for a change"!

00:23.996 --> 00:25.731
What have you got there?

00:25.731 --> 00:27.290
Oh, this?

00:28.667 --> 00:30.302
"Miyamoto research room"?

00:30.302 --> 00:32.238
Did you make your own research room?

00:32.238 --> 00:32.571
Did you make your own research room?

00:32.571 --> 00:33.272
Yup!

00:33.272 --> 00:36.942
When I discussed it with the school principal,
he happened to have a vacant room, so...

00:36.942 --> 00:38.043
I see...

00:38.043 --> 00:41.881
Hey, Becky, you said it's a research room,
SO are you going to research something?

00:41.881 --> 00:42.715
Yeah.

00:42.715 --> 00:45.651
What are you going to research?
Tell me, tell me!

00:45.651 --> 00:46.652
That's a secret.

00:46.652 --> 00:48.687
I'm so curious!

00:48.687 --> 00:50.456
I wonder what kind of research it could be...

00:50.456 --> 00:50.523
Maho, maho, maho...

00:50.523 --> 00:51.624
Maho, maho, maho...

00:51.624 --> 00:51.988
Maho, maho, maho...

01:03.135 --> 01:04.830
If I drink this...

01:12.978 --> 01:15.047
Yes, it worked!

01:15.047 --> 01:17.141
Hooray, hooray, hooray!

01:19.285 --> 01:21.987
Mahoho, I want one of those...

01:21.987 --> 01:24.523
Looks like she's imagining something weird...

01:24.523 --> 01:26.992
Himeko, that's not it at all.

01:26.992 --> 01:27.259
What? It's not?

01:27.259 --> 01:27.927
What? It's not?

01:27.927 --> 01:28.294
What? It's not?

01:28.294 --> 01:29.528
Then...

01:29.528 --> 01:29.995
Maho, maho, maho, maho...

01:29.995 --> 01:31.096
Maho, maho, maho, maho...

01:31.096 --> 01:31.119
Maho, maho, maho, maho...

01:35.734 --> 01:37.395
If I drink this...

01:46.045 --> 01:48.878
It finally worked!

01:50.216 --> 01:52.151
Mahoho...

01:52.151 --> 01:54.353
Oh, my Becky...

01:54.353 --> 01:58.090
Give me back my Becky!

01:58.090 --> 01:59.124
Should we leave her alone?

01:59.124 --> 02:00.059
Let's do that.

02:00.626 --> 02:03.362
Loose ni koi suru otome wa

02:03.362 --> 02:06.098
Diamond de mabushii

02:06.098 --> 02:11.604
Tat you carat ranhansha no kisetsu yo pichi pichi

02:11.604 --> 02:14.139
Oh nami ban ba ban ban!

02:14.139 --> 02:17.076
Doko wo mite iru no yo

02:17.076 --> 02:21.411
Oshiri cute de kurakura shiteru no ne

02:22.681 --> 02:25.551
Rose wa abunai pheromone

02:25.551 --> 02:28.287
Kocchi wo muitara ichikoro

02:28.287 --> 02:33.826
Wink kiratto daisansha no kisetsu yo sexy!

02:33.826 --> 02:36.528
Oh nami ban ba ban ban!

02:36.528 --> 02:39.331
Nani wo shite iru no yo

02:39.331 --> 02:43.802
Kono miryoku ni kizukanai

02:43.802 --> 02:49.832
Nanohana kaze ni yurete

02:50.109 --> 02:54.880
Watashi mo kaze ni naru

02:54.880 --> 03:01.220
Nanohana temaneki wo shite

03:01.220 --> 03:03.889
Mitsubachi kisugi da wa

03:03.889 --> 03:06.586
Chotto kiken na kanji

03:07.126 --> 03:11.290
Bun bun bu bu bun kiiroi bakansu yo

03:12.698 --> 03:16.862
Bun bun bu bu bun kiiroi bakansu yo

03:18.270 --> 03:22.434
Bun bun bu bu bun kiiroi bakansu yo

03:23.709 --> 03:26.378
Bun bun bu bu bun kiiroi bakansu yo

03:26.378 --> 03:28.047
Bun bun bu bu bun kiiroi bakansu yo

03:32.084 --> 03:34.853
What made you decide to get a research room
all of a sudden, anyway?

03:34.853 --> 03:36.822
I wanted to have my own hideout at school.

03:36.822 --> 03:37.389
I wanted to have my own hideout at school.

03:37.389 --> 03:38.490
Hideout?

03:38.490 --> 03:40.960
I know this is a workplace,

03:40.960 --> 03:43.295
but this school is filled with distractions,

03:43.295 --> 03:46.065
and it's hard for me to think about things clearly.

03:46.065 --> 03:48.233
Well, I guess you could say

03:48.233 --> 03:50.793
I wanted a room where I can be me.

03:50.970 --> 03:52.404
Hmm, I see.

03:52.404 --> 03:53.572
They don't call you a genius for nothing, huh?

03:53.572 --> 03:56.375
Look at how argumentatively you think
about stuff. Pretty impressive.

03:56.375 --> 03:58.444
Don't say "argumentatively."

03:58.444 --> 04:00.242
It doesn't sound very flattering.

04:03.749 --> 04:04.550
So is this it?

04:04.550 --> 04:05.417
Yeah.

04:05.417 --> 04:07.720
They told me it's been vacant ever since
they opened this school.

04:07.720 --> 04:08.949
Come on, let's go in!

04:13.826 --> 04:15.260
Is it time to pay a bill?

04:15.260 --> 04:16.921
Sorry to bother you.

04:19.031 --> 04:20.733
People live in there.

04:20.733 --> 04:23.335
I'll go ask him to give me a different room.

04:23.335 --> 04:24.603
That's a good idea.

04:27.373 --> 04:29.641
Body temperature: 38 degrees Celsius...

04:29.641 --> 04:32.077
There's been no change for the last hour.

04:32.077 --> 04:35.147
Captain, I understand it's very
peaceful around here,

04:35.147 --> 04:36.949
but I think this is totally pointless.

04:36.949 --> 04:38.283
Just shut up and do it.

04:38.283 --> 04:41.987
Like I said, we should go ahead
and invite Miss Miyamoto here,

04:41.987 --> 04:44.089
since she is the target of our study after all.

04:44.089 --> 04:49.995
Direct contact with intelligent life from the planet
which is under observation is forbidden!

04:49.995 --> 04:51.397
Don't tell me you've forgotten that.

04:51.397 --> 04:53.465
Of course not...

04:53.465 --> 04:55.667
Of course not, but still...

04:55.667 --> 05:00.195
doing research on stuff
like this is totally pointless!

05:01.874 --> 05:03.364
I'm the Lord, meow.

05:04.143 --> 05:07.613
All right! Today we'll continue
our discussion of quadratic functions.

05:07.613 --> 05:08.614
Becky!

05:08.614 --> 05:10.049
What is it, Rei?

05:10.049 --> 05:11.817
So what's the deal with your research room?

05:11.817 --> 05:15.412
Oh, the principal gave me another vacant room.

05:15.721 --> 05:16.688
Maho!

05:16.688 --> 05:18.624
Let's go check it out!

05:18.624 --> 05:20.492
I'll help you organize your room!

05:20.492 --> 05:22.895
Shut up! You can do that AFTER class!

05:22.895 --> 05:24.430
Shut up, you bookworm.

05:24.430 --> 05:25.697
Don't call me a worm!

05:25.697 --> 05:27.399
Come on, let's go, Becky.

05:27.399 --> 05:28.867
Now is the time to act!

05:28.867 --> 05:33.138
I'll be in trouble if they see me walking around
school with a bunch of students during class!

05:33.138 --> 05:33.272
I'll be in trouble if they see me walking around
school with a bunch of students during class!

05:33.272 --> 05:34.673
Don't worry! I'll protect you, Becky!

05:34.673 --> 05:36.241
Don't worry! I'll protect you, Becky!

05:36.241 --> 05:39.302
Ah, that's not the point, Himeko!

05:43.449 --> 05:45.317
So it's study hall.

05:45.317 --> 05:46.051
Ichijo!

05:46.051 --> 05:46.251
Ichijo!

05:52.558 --> 05:54.760
D-Did you just see that?

05:54.760 --> 05:57.096
Yeah, but it's Ichijo
we're talking about, so...

05:57.096 --> 05:58.263
Is that all there is to it?

05:58.263 --> 05:58.786
Is that all there is to it?

05:59.364 --> 06:00.354
It's study hall.

06:05.204 --> 06:06.899
Whoa!

06:07.673 --> 06:09.641
That's my Otome!

06:09.641 --> 06:10.733
Thanks!

06:11.743 --> 06:13.645
All right, next! Shiratori!

06:13.645 --> 06:15.814
Hey, Shiratori!

06:15.814 --> 06:17.578
You're Shiratori!

06:20.352 --> 06:23.117
I-I'm Shiratori No. 2.

06:23.822 --> 06:26.291
All right, No. 2! Go!

06:26.458 --> 06:27.289
What?

06:27.693 --> 06:29.294
I can't...

06:29.294 --> 06:33.424
Hey now, you can't give up before you even try!

06:35.701 --> 06:37.169
I-I'll do my best.

06:37.169 --> 06:40.298
I'll do my best, so please help me.

06:40.539 --> 06:42.674
All right, let's do this!

06:42.674 --> 06:44.109
Don't get outdone by Otome!

06:44.109 --> 06:45.702
O-Okay...

06:46.645 --> 06:49.148
I can... I can fly!

06:49.148 --> 06:52.015
I'm a bird, that's right, I'm a bird!

07:01.527 --> 07:03.095
I'm sorry...

07:03.095 --> 07:06.365
I couldn't meet your expectations after all...

07:06.365 --> 07:08.600
What are you talking about, Saotome?

07:08.600 --> 07:11.695
Like I said, you need to call me
MISTER Saotome!

07:12.971 --> 07:15.997
Obviously I'm not even here...

07:19.511 --> 07:21.570
I, um...

07:22.748 --> 07:25.911
Hey, Mr. Saotome, let's play dodgeball next!

07:26.518 --> 07:29.621
Or portball or discus!

07:29.621 --> 07:31.111
Oh no...

07:37.496 --> 07:39.965
I've never been inside the
old school building before.

07:42.034 --> 07:44.836
I didn't even know it existed until today.

07:44.836 --> 07:46.772
Man, this is creepy.

07:46.772 --> 07:48.140
Totally.

07:48.140 --> 07:50.404
This is the creepy of the year.

07:52.244 --> 07:54.813
Do you think a ghost will show up? Do you?

07:54.813 --> 07:56.682
Maho, maho, maho!

07:56.682 --> 07:58.446
Don't look so happy saying that!

07:58.684 --> 08:00.953
Oh, let me guess, you're scared, Miyako?

08:00.953 --> 08:02.688
N-No way I'm scared!

08:02.688 --> 08:05.157
First of all, why did you even come with us?

08:05.157 --> 08:07.359
A bookworm should go back to the
classroom and study by herself.

08:07.359 --> 08:08.860
Don't you call me a worm!

08:08.860 --> 08:11.630
But, seriously, what do we do if
a ghost shows up for real?

08:11.630 --> 08:13.131
Don't worry.

08:13.131 --> 08:14.900
We have Ichijo on our side.

08:14.900 --> 08:16.201
I see!

08:16.201 --> 08:18.568
We're counting on you, Ichijo.

08:18.770 --> 08:19.638
She's not here!

08:19.638 --> 08:21.206
But she was with us the whole time!

08:21.206 --> 08:23.402
Don't tell me this is the work of a ghost?!

08:35.087 --> 08:36.154
Whoa!

08:39.324 --> 08:41.893
Um, Miss Watanuki.

08:41.893 --> 08:43.495
What?

08:43.495 --> 08:45.764
Why are you skipping class?

08:45.764 --> 08:48.066
Is this a so-called counterintelligence activity?

08:48.066 --> 08:50.402
I don't like exercising.

08:50.402 --> 08:54.640
Hey, I heard that the little kid teacher from 1-C
has made her own research room,

08:54.640 --> 08:57.175
but have you heard any
mysterious rumors about that?

08:57.175 --> 08:59.077
So you wanna discover the mystery?

08:59.077 --> 09:00.412
I don't know if I want to DISCOVER it,

09:00.412 --> 09:02.047
it's more like I want to investigate it...

09:02.047 --> 09:02.914
Huh?!

09:02.914 --> 09:04.040
Who was that just now?

09:05.617 --> 09:08.780
Then seek it. The truth is out there.

09:11.556 --> 09:15.861
Hey, Miss Watanuki! What happened?
No more skipping class?

09:15.861 --> 09:18.397
All of a sudden, I feel like exercising.

09:23.468 --> 09:25.137
There's nothing but junk in here.

09:25.137 --> 09:27.673
This is so normal. It's kinda boring!

09:27.673 --> 09:30.008
Well, I guess that's the reality.

09:30.008 --> 09:33.245
All right then, I guess I'm going back
to the classroom to study!

09:33.245 --> 09:34.379
Wait.

09:34.379 --> 09:35.447
Let me go!

09:35.447 --> 09:39.584
It'll be YOUR fault if I fail the
college exam and my life is ruined!

09:39.584 --> 09:42.487
Can't you give me a better excuse than that?

09:42.487 --> 09:44.823
Anyway, we want you to help us
clean up this place.

09:44.823 --> 09:45.517
NO!

09:49.861 --> 09:52.397
It's all right. You don't have to
force yourself to help us.

09:52.397 --> 09:54.032
We're supposed to be in class
right now to begin with.

09:54.032 --> 09:57.936
And besides, this clean-up is to make
this my personal research room, anyway.

09:57.936 --> 10:02.207
Whoa! Miss Miyamoto, you're
the adult of the year!

10:02.207 --> 10:03.942
Becky, you're cool!

10:03.942 --> 10:05.911
Well, if you say so...

10:05.911 --> 10:07.572
Go back to the classroom.

10:07.879 --> 10:09.608
Miyako, good luck on your studying!

10:10.582 --> 10:12.050
Good luck to you, Miss Miyako!

10:12.818 --> 10:14.616
I know you'll be accepted to a
prestigious college!

10:15.387 --> 10:16.445
Well, Miyako...

10:18.056 --> 10:19.958
How am I supposed to go back now?!

10:19.958 --> 10:20.726
Huh?

10:20.726 --> 10:22.761
Huh? What's wrong, Miyako?

10:22.761 --> 10:23.922
A door.

10:24.730 --> 10:25.964
Hey, she's right!

10:25.964 --> 10:28.133
Maho! It's a mystery!

10:28.133 --> 10:29.901
I wonder what the door is for.

10:29.901 --> 10:31.603
It bugs me...

10:31.603 --> 10:33.338
It sure bugs me, but...

10:33.338 --> 10:35.941
I don't think we should open it.

10:35.941 --> 10:37.242
Yeah.

10:37.242 --> 10:39.074
Let's just pretend we didn't see it.

10:41.646 --> 10:43.014
Miss Ichijo?

10:43.014 --> 10:43.105
Miss Ichijo?

10:44.282 --> 10:45.750
Don't do it, Ichijo!

10:47.652 --> 10:48.720
MAHO!

10:48.720 --> 10:50.347
She opened it!

10:55.560 --> 10:57.129
N-No way!

10:57.129 --> 10:58.062
Wh-Why?

11:01.032 --> 11:02.033
Yeeeeeeeeeeeek!

11:02.033 --> 11:02.768
Yeeeeeeeeeeeek!

11:02.768 --> 11:03.535
Yeeeeeeeeeeeek!

11:03.535 --> 11:05.537
Yeeeeeeeeeeeek!

11:05.537 --> 11:07.773
Yeeeeeeeeeeeek!

11:07.773 --> 11:09.969
Yeeeeeeeeeeeek!

11:18.250 --> 11:20.752
She got it! All right, go, Suzune!

11:20.752 --> 11:22.587
Okay, here I go!

11:22.587 --> 11:24.612
Give it all you've got!

11:24.923 --> 11:26.516
Okay!

11:30.729 --> 11:31.696
What?

11:31.696 --> 11:33.031
You just aimed at me, didn't you?

11:33.031 --> 11:36.368
Aim? At you? Why would I do that?

11:36.368 --> 11:39.504
I'm on your side! Don't get it mixed up, all right?

11:39.504 --> 11:41.606
What makes you think I'd get it mixed up?

11:41.606 --> 11:42.266
Hmph.

11:46.411 --> 11:48.346
Like I said!

11:48.346 --> 11:50.015
I didn't do anything.

11:50.015 --> 11:51.483
I can just feel the violence!

11:51.483 --> 11:53.618
I wasn't going to do anything violent!

11:53.618 --> 11:55.520
That's enough! Just give me the ball!

11:55.520 --> 11:56.721
Why?

11:56.721 --> 11:57.956
Just give it to me!

11:57.956 --> 11:58.857
Boo!

11:58.857 --> 11:59.825
Come on, now!

11:59.825 --> 12:01.384
Here.

12:16.641 --> 12:18.439
Man, I thought I was going to die.

12:19.211 --> 12:21.009
That was omega-close, wasn't it?

12:21.780 --> 12:23.680
Thank god Miss Ichijo was with us.

12:24.449 --> 12:26.349
She was the one who opened it, though...

12:29.721 --> 12:32.122
Hey, where is Miss Ichijo?

12:33.859 --> 12:35.460
Did we put her up there with them?

12:35.460 --> 12:37.986
No way...

12:42.334 --> 12:44.860
But if that is the case,
what are we going to do?!

12:45.337 --> 12:47.863
Then let's open it and find out.

12:49.875 --> 12:50.865
She's right here.

12:58.183 --> 12:59.584
C-Captain!

12:59.584 --> 13:02.320
Wh-What? I wasn't sleeping, you know!

13:02.320 --> 13:03.989
Did you just see that?!

13:03.989 --> 13:05.223
See what?

13:05.223 --> 13:08.022
This huge hand turned the Earth!!

13:08.393 --> 13:10.919
What are you blabbering about?

13:11.696 --> 13:14.688
What am I blabbering about?
I see, I must've been dreaming...

13:15.467 --> 13:16.635
Captain, look!

13:16.635 --> 13:19.070
Pink, pink...

13:19.070 --> 13:21.596
Hey, you just saw that, too, didn't you?

13:24.509 --> 13:25.977
It was you, wasn't it?

13:26.444 --> 13:28.246
I'm the Lord, meow.

13:33.118 --> 13:35.120
I finally finished cleaning it up.

13:35.120 --> 13:37.455
It took me a whole week, though...

13:37.455 --> 13:40.725
And for some reason your memories
during that time are blurry, aren't they?

13:40.725 --> 13:43.695
Boy, being alone sure is relaxing!

13:43.695 --> 13:45.424
But I'm here, too...

13:46.498 --> 13:47.988
Hmm? Come in!

13:48.867 --> 13:51.236
Oh, Ichijo, what's up?

13:51.236 --> 13:52.635
I've come to congratulate you.

13:52.804 --> 13:54.139
Congratulate me?

13:54.139 --> 13:57.234
Congratulations on the opening of
your counseling room.

13:57.742 --> 14:00.178
Well, that's not exactly right.
But thanks anyway.

14:00.178 --> 14:02.180
I've brought some presents.

14:02.180 --> 14:02.213
I've brought some presents.

14:02.213 --> 14:03.081
Really?

14:03.081 --> 14:05.617
A golden human phantom or
a silver funerary urn,

14:05.617 --> 14:07.385
which one would you like?

14:07.385 --> 14:08.787
I don't want either one.

14:08.787 --> 14:10.956
Then how about a copper
adulterous affair novel?

14:10.956 --> 14:12.090
I don't want it.

14:12.090 --> 14:14.292
It's a bestseller.

14:14.292 --> 14:16.556
Please get out of here.

14:18.630 --> 14:20.065
Someone else came.

14:20.065 --> 14:21.260
Yeah?

14:22.133 --> 14:23.658
Kurumi?

14:24.769 --> 14:27.005
Becky, listen to my problem!

14:27.005 --> 14:29.507
I was... I was called plain again!

14:29.507 --> 14:32.177
To make it even worse,
I was called plain by Miss Itou from 1-B!

14:32.177 --> 14:35.147
Like I said, this isn't a counseling room...

14:39.184 --> 14:41.453
That's Rei's writing. That rat!

14:43.121 --> 14:44.623
Becky!

14:44.623 --> 14:46.758
I was so shocked to be called that by Miss Itou!

14:46.758 --> 14:47.025
I was so shocked to be called that by Miss Itou!

14:47.025 --> 14:48.660
Aargh, you're so annoying!

14:48.660 --> 14:50.526
Who the hell is "Miss Itou" anyway?!

14:54.866 --> 15:01.039
Anyway, a story can't make sense without
explaining what happened, how, and when.

15:01.039 --> 15:05.176
So telling the listener the words you want to
convey isn't enough to get the point across.

15:05.176 --> 15:08.346
Excuse me! Otome said
she wants a research room!

15:08.346 --> 15:08.413
I didn't say that!

15:08.413 --> 15:10.115
I didn't say that!

15:10.115 --> 15:10.415
I didn't say that!

15:10.415 --> 15:11.249
See?

15:11.249 --> 15:12.217
Huh?

15:12.217 --> 15:16.955
All right, remembering what we just talked about,
Watanuki, read starting at page 55!

15:16.955 --> 15:18.223
Yes, sir!

15:18.223 --> 15:19.357
Let's see...

15:19.357 --> 15:23.762
"The governor of Connecticut felt frustration
towards the governor of Saitama Prefecture,

15:23.762 --> 15:26.732
who only kept nodding and didn't look like
he was going to share his opinion at all."

15:27.098 --> 15:29.401
Come on, stand up when you read.

15:29.401 --> 15:30.669
I am standing.

15:30.669 --> 15:31.932
Huh?

15:32.003 --> 15:33.738
Who the heck are you?

15:33.738 --> 15:33.872
Hibiki Watanuki of 1-B, kero.

15:33.872 --> 15:34.472
Hibiki Watanuki of 1-B, kero.

15:34.472 --> 15:35.106
Hibiki Watanuki of 1-B, kero.

15:35.106 --> 15:35.507
Hibiki Watanuki of 1-B, kero.

15:35.507 --> 15:35.907
Hibiki Watanuki of 1-B, kero.

15:35.907 --> 15:36.430
Hibiki Watanuki of 1-B, kero.

15:37.108 --> 15:37.242
OUT!

15:37.242 --> 15:37.800
OUT!

15:46.317 --> 15:49.387
Now we're going into the little kid
teacher's research room!

15:49.387 --> 15:52.590
It's smaller than I expected,
but neatly organized.

15:52.590 --> 15:53.024
It's smaller than I expected,
but neatly organized.

15:53.024 --> 15:55.927
But whether it was done by
the little kid teacher herself

15:55.927 --> 15:58.897
or by students who helped
her clean is unknown!

15:58.897 --> 16:00.899
Hmm? I found something on the desk!

16:00.899 --> 16:01.127
Hmm? I found something on the desk!

16:02.000 --> 16:04.469
It's an open bag of potato chips!

16:04.469 --> 16:07.439
It's not finished, but was left here
without being sealed properly!

16:07.439 --> 16:09.641
I assume it belongs to the little kid teacher,

16:09.641 --> 16:13.278
and it is indeed evidence that reveals
her careless personality!

16:13.278 --> 16:17.237
Judging from this, I suspect that this room
has been organized by her students!

16:17.382 --> 16:18.349
Huh?

16:18.516 --> 16:20.418
I found a door on the ceiling!

16:20.418 --> 16:22.520
It's been closed off very securely!

16:22.520 --> 16:25.290
Could it be the little kid teacher's secret room?

16:25.290 --> 16:28.860
I am now going to open this secret door!

16:32.931 --> 16:35.457
Class is over.

16:35.867 --> 16:36.935
It's all right.

16:36.935 --> 16:40.505
I'm sure no one's even realized that I'm gone.

16:40.505 --> 16:43.808
I don't think so, but I'm sure that's
the case with me though.

16:43.808 --> 16:47.369
No... I'm less noticeable than you...

16:54.385 --> 16:58.049
I'm tired. I think I'll relax in my research room.

16:58.923 --> 16:59.524
Huh?

16:59.524 --> 16:59.924
Huh?

17:06.197 --> 17:08.859
Did I leave the door open when I left?

17:10.635 --> 17:12.070
Can I have a moment with you?

17:12.070 --> 17:15.340
Sure. You're the twin from 1-Al
Are you the older sister?

17:15.340 --> 17:16.708
I'm the younger one.

17:16.708 --> 17:19.310
Oh, the easy-going one, right? What's up?

17:19.310 --> 17:21.146
It's about my sister...

17:21.146 --> 17:23.515
Oh, you want me to listen to your problem.

17:23.515 --> 17:26.718
For stuff like that, I suggest you talk to
your homeroom teacher, Miss lgarashi.

17:26.718 --> 17:29.854
Miss Miyamoto! Yuma is so mean!

17:29.854 --> 17:31.322
You're just not listening to me, are you?

17:31.322 --> 17:35.527
At yesterday's audition, we managed
to stay in until the end, but...

17:35.527 --> 17:36.961
Audition?

17:36.961 --> 17:38.029
For what?

17:38.029 --> 17:39.330
To become a pop idol!

17:39.330 --> 17:40.126
Oh...

17:43.468 --> 17:48.872
I'm Yuna Kashiwagi, 16 years old.
I'm a freshman at high school.

17:49.140 --> 17:51.976
All right, let's ask you a few questions.

17:51.976 --> 17:53.912
Hmm? Miss Kashiwagi.

17:53.912 --> 17:55.180
Yes?

17:55.180 --> 17:57.315
You've got something written on your arm.

17:57.315 --> 17:59.083
Look, on your upper arm.

17:59.083 --> 18:00.185
What?

18:06.357 --> 18:09.694
Isn't it horrible? Isn't it atrocious?

18:09.694 --> 18:11.095
You haven't seen anything yet.

18:11.095 --> 18:14.132
My sister, on the other hand, would do
something much worse, without remorse.

18:14.132 --> 18:15.767
Really? Like what?

18:15.767 --> 18:17.669
Hmm, let's see...

18:17.669 --> 18:19.763
The other day... Look...

18:21.005 --> 18:23.702
U-Unbelievable!

18:24.075 --> 18:25.777
Thank you, Miss Miyamoto!

18:25.777 --> 18:28.712
Thanks to you, I feel
so much better now! Bye-bye!

18:30.014 --> 18:32.073
Oh boy...

18:33.251 --> 18:34.552
Here comes another one...

18:34.552 --> 18:35.678
Yeah?

18:36.821 --> 18:39.222
You're from 1-D...

18:40.291 --> 18:42.020
What was that about?

18:42.327 --> 18:43.351
Yeah?

18:44.529 --> 18:47.760
Miyata, if you want to speak to me,
just spit it out!

18:48.533 --> 18:51.161
If she does that again,
she's gonna pay for it!

18:52.070 --> 18:53.094
Yeah?!

18:54.172 --> 18:56.334
If you close the door, I'll put a hole in it.

18:56.941 --> 18:59.842
I'm... clumsy.

19:00.345 --> 19:03.508
What do you think I can do
to correct that, Miss Miyamoto?

19:04.549 --> 19:04.616
You're right. You are impressively clumsy.

19:04.616 --> 19:04.949
You're right. You are impressively clumsy.

